}</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-12">
            <div class="card mb-4">
                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">GetNum3Func</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h6>Description:</h6>
                    <p>A function that takes a string parameter and returns a number based on the input value. 
                    Demonstrates parameter handling, validation, and conditional logic.</p>
                    
                    <h6>Parameters:</h6>
                    <ul>
                        <li><code>param1</code> (String): Input string to evaluate</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <h6>Returns:</h6>
                    <ul>
                        <li><code>3.0</code> if the parameter equals "ABC" (case-insensitive)</li>
                        <li><code>0.0</code> for any other value</li>
                    </ul>
                    
                    <h6>Usage Examples:</h6>
                    <div class="row">
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <pre class="bg-light p-3"><code>return GetNum3Func('ABC')</code></pre>
                            <p><strong>Result:</strong> 3</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="col-md-6">
                            <pre class="bg-light p-3"><code>return GetNum3Func('XYZ')</code></pre>
                            <p><strong>Result:</strong> 0</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    
                    <h6>Complex Example:</h6>
                    <pre class="bg-light p-3"><code>return Max(GetNum1Func(), GetNum2Func()) * GetNum3Func('ABC')</code></pre>
                    <p><strong>Result:</strong> 6 (Max of 1 and 2 is 2, multiplied by 3)</p>
                    
                    <h6>Source Code:</h6>
                    <pre class="bg-dark text-light p-3" style="font-size: 0.85em;"><code>public class GetNum3Func : BaseFunction
{
    public GetNum3Func() : base(nameof(GetNum3Func), 1)
    {
    }

    public override IValue Execute()
    {
        // Validate parameter count
        if (Params.Count() != 1)
        {
            throw new Exception("GetNum3Func expects exactly one parameter.");
        }

        // Validate parameter type
        if (Params.Any(x => !x.Is&lt;string&gt;()))
        {
            throw new Exception("GetNum3Func expects a string parameter.");
        }

        // Get the first parameter
        var firstParam = Params.First();
        var paramValue = firstParam.As&lt;string&gt;();

        // Return different values based on input
        return paramValue.Equals("ABC", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase) 
            ? new Value(3.0) 
            : new Value(0.0);
    }
}</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="card mb-4">
        <div class="card-header bg-dark text-white">
            <h5 class="mb-0">How to Create Your Own Custom Function</h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            <h6>Step 1: Create a class that extends BaseFunction</h6>
            <pre class="bg-light p-3"><code>using RecipeCalculator.Common.Function;
using RecipeCalculator.Common.Values;

public class MyCustomFunc : BaseFunction
{
    // Constructor: name and parameter count
    public MyCustomFunc() : base(nameof(MyCustomFunc), 1)
    {
    }

    public override IValue Execute()
    {
        // Your logic here
        // Access parameters via: Params
        // Return: new Value(result)
        return new Value(42.0);
    }
}</code></pre>
            
            <h6 class="mt-3">Step 2: Register the function when executing formulas</h6>
            <p>Custom functions are passed to the <code>EngineRunner.Execute()</code> method:</p>
            <pre class="bg-light p-3"><code>var functions = new IFunction[] 
{ 
    new GetNum1Func(), 
    new GetNum2Func(), 
    new GetNum3Func() 
};

EngineRunner.Execute(formulas, functions);</code></pre>
            
            <h6 class="mt-3">Step 3: Use in formulas</h6>
            <pre class="bg-light p-3"><code>return MyCustomFunc(parameter)</code></pre>
            
            <h6 class="mt-3">Key Points:</h6>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Constructor parameters:</strong> Function name and expected parameter count</li>
                <li><strong>Params property:</strong> Access function parameters (IEnumerable&lt;IValue&gt;)</li>
                <li><strong>Type checking:</strong> Use <code>param.Is&lt;T&gt;()</code> and <code>param.As&lt;T&gt;()</code></li>
                <li><strong>Return value:</strong> Must return <code>IValue</code> (wrap with <code>new Value()</code>)</li>
                <li><strong>Supported types:</strong> double, string, bool</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <div class="card">
        <div class="card-header bg-warning">
            <h5 class="mb-0">Try It Yourself</h5>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body">
            <p>Go to the <a href="/">Formula Calculator</a> and try these examples:</p>
            
            <div class="mb-3">
                <strong>Example 1: Basic Usage</strong>
                <pre class="bg-light p-2"><code>return GetNum1Func() + GetNum2Func()</code></pre>
                <small class="text-muted">Expected Result: 3</small>
            </div>
            
            <div class="mb-3">
                <strong>Example 2: With Built-in Functions</strong>
                <pre class="bg-light p-2"><code>return Max(GetNum1Func(), GetNum2Func())</code></pre>
                <small class="text-muted">Expected Result: 2</small>
            </div>
            
            <div class="mb-3">
                <strong>Example 3: With Parameters</strong>
                <pre class="bg-light p-2"><code>return GetNum3Func('ABC') + GetNum3Func('XYZ')</code></pre>
                <small class="text-muted">Expected Result: 3 (3 + 0)</small>
            </div>
            
            <div class="mb-3">
                <strong>Example 4: Complex Expression</strong>
                <pre class="bg-light p-2"><code>return Max(GetNum1Func(), GetNum2Func()) * GetNum3Func('ABC')</code></pre>
                <small class="text-muted">Expected Result: 6</small>
            </div>
            
            <div class="mb-3">
                <strong>Example 5: With Conditionals</strong>
                <pre class="bg-light p-2"><code>if (GetNum3Func('ABC') > 0) then
  return GetNum1Func() + GetNum2Func()
else
  return 0
end</code></pre>
                <small class="text-muted">Expected Result: 3</small>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
